# macOS application Quit ownership

Branch: `macos-quit-lifecycle`; candidate: `1.0.123-macos-quit-lifecycle`.

The operator accepted 1.0.122's Command-Q behavior, then requested removal of
the contributed Quit bridge. Preserve that candidate/branch as a checkpoint.
Remove only the bridge introduced after 1.0.120; do not reset the repository,
discard dependency-cache work, or remove the tested shortcut-ownership guard.

## Contract

- Captured Command-Q belongs exclusively to the remote session. Retain the
  native Quit-key-equivalent guard and its focus/capture restoration tests.
- Explicit menu/Dock Quit is application exit, not a synthetic SDL disconnect.
  A macOS QGuiApplication subclass handles the normal Qt Quit event, requests
  session cancellation once, and defers normal Qt exit until cleanup completes.
- Register ownership before session initialization. Release it on queued
  readyForDeletion, not sessionFinished (which precedes transport cleanup).
  Account for a new session overlapping an old deferred cleanup.
- The session cancels startup/takeover/reconnect through existing cancellation
  flags. Its explicit application-exit flag terminates the SDL loop, even if
  the Host sends no events. No new SDL Quit injection or process-global filter.
- Toolbar/window disconnect still returns to the host list. Application Quit
  suppresses that intermediate navigation and exits only after resources stop.
- Linux application ownership, Host, transport and protocol are unchanged.

## Validation

Every Mac build runs the existing native shortcut tests plus isolated real-Qt
application lifetimes: idle Quit, active cancellation, repeated Quit, ordinary
disconnect, failed startup and overlapping deferred cleanup. Root source guards
check platform scope and completion-signal wiring. These do not simulate a live
network or prove menu/Dock behavior in an active desktop session.

Build/sign/notarize on GitHub-hosted macOS27, retaining exact source and hashes.
Operator gate: captured Command-Q quits only the remote app; menu and Dock Quit
close PLANK while streaming and during reconnect; disconnect keeps PLANK open;
idle/capture-disabled Command-Q quits locally. Do not merge before acceptance.

## Candidate result

Signed hosted run 35185783350 passed at root
`be387875a3fde8dd87c5a3b4c046d368f1a58457`, Client
`be8a1e06cba05299f939cea2bc4f440bef1a9196`. All seven native shortcut and six
application-lifetime cases passed, alongside existing suites. Dependency cache
restored and verified; signing, notarization and Gatekeeper passed. Exact
package/hash are in HANDOFF. The operator accepted the candidate and authorized
merge, mainline rebuild and publication as 1.0.124. No agent deployment.

The initial run 35185516514 compiled the application but caught a test relying
on the deleted bridge's transitive SDL include. The test now includes SDL
directly; no package or weakened gate resulted from that failed attempt.
